# Keep the build context small + reproducible. target/ is huge and host-arch;
# .git and local scratch never belong in an image build.
target/
**/target/
.git/
**/*.rs.bk
*.log

# CREDENTIAL EXCLUSIONS. Every Dockerfile here does `COPY . .` from the repo root,
# and the CodeBuild path additionally uploads the whole tree to S3 as source.zip —
# so anything reachable from the context lands in a pushed image layer, readable by
# every principal with registry pull rights.
#
# `work/` is where the runbooks and the `scripts/test-*-cloud.sh.example` headers
# tell an operator to keep FILLED-IN cloud credential scripts, precisely because it
# is gitignored. That also makes `tracked_secrets_gate.py` blind to it by
# construction: that gate scans TRACKED files. This list is the only thing standing
# between those files and a published image.
work/
**/work/
# Local agent and editor state. `.claude/` is TRACKED here, so unlike `work/` it is not
# even gitignored — `COPY . .` picks it up unconditionally, and
# `.claude/settings.local.json` is where env vars and MCP server tokens live while the
# skill tree next to it holds private review material. `.verification/` is local lane
# scratch. These landed in `.gcloudignore` and not here, and the parity control that was
# supposed to notice was a fixed list that did not name them.
.claude/
**/.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.verification/
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*-seed
**/*seed.txt
**/kubeconfig
.aws/
.gcloud/
.kube/

# LOCAL RUNTIME TREES. Every Dockerfile here does `COPY . .`, so these are copied into
# the build context, into the builder layer, and — for the CodeBuild path — into the
# uploaded source.zip. They are none of them inputs to any image.
#
# They are also LARGE, and that is not a tidiness point: the four Node lines the
# TypeScript runtime matrix installs (~780 MB) plus the seven Python venvs (~550 MB) plus
# `node_modules` (~155 MB) took the proxy build's context from ~90 MB to 1.62 GB, and the
# Docker VM ran out of disk mid-`COPY` — which fails the fleet lane at image build, before
# a single security proof runs. A build context that grows with the local toolchain matrix
# makes the acceptance gate depend on how many runtimes the developer happens to have
# installed.
#
# The matrices themselves are correct and stay: `scripts/prepare_node_matrix.sh` and
# `scripts/prepare_python_matrix.sh` install them so a battery is measured on every
# supported runtime. They belong beside the SDK sources and not inside an image.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.venv*/
**/.venv*/
sdk/typescript/.node-v*/
**/__pycache__/
